Introduction to phishing 
Phishing is a type of cyberattack where criminals use fake messages, emails, phone calls that pretend to come fro trusted company or person to trick you into giving away sensitive information.
Types of phishing
Email phishing : bulk fradulent emails sent to thousands of people hoping someone falls for the trick.
Spear phishing : targeted attacks aimed at a specific individual or organization using personalized details.
Smishing : phishing conducted via SMS text messages.
Vishing : voice phishing via telephone calls.
Pretexeting : fabricating a scenario to extract sensitive information.
How to prevent phishing.
